---
source: tests/help.rs
expression: "help_for(dir.path(), &[noun])"
---
Shell completion script

Usage: cdctl completions [OPTIONS] <SHELL>

Arguments:
  <SHELL>
          [possible values: bash, elvish, fish, powershell, zsh]

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Global options:
  -p, --profile <PK|name>
          Profile to operate on (name or PK) [env: CONTROLD_PROFILE]

      --json
          Emit JSON (full document) instead of a table

      --fields <a,b>
          Comma-separated JSON fields to keep (implies --json)

      --plain
          Tables without borders, for awk/cut

  -y, --yes
          Skip confirmation prompts (ignored when the target profile is implicit)

      --no-retry
          Disable automatic retries

      --timeout <SECS>
          Per-request timeout in seconds

      --debug
          Request/response trace on stderr (token always redacted)

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress info lines on stderr (warnings and errors still print)

Install:
  bash  cdctl completions bash > ~/.local/share/bash-completion/completions/cdctl
  zsh   cdctl completions zsh > ~/.zfunc/_cdctl   (add fpath+=~/.zfunc before compinit)
  fish  cdctl completions fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/cdctl.fish

Create the target directory first if missing (mkdir -p). Open a new shell afterwards. Regenerate
after upgrading cdctl.
